WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/system/components/status/TeslaAuthCard.tsx — a PURE presentational component (no hooks,
  no fetch). Its parent (SystemStatusPage) feeds three props: `authenticated: boolean | undefined`,
  `expiresAt: string | undefined`, and a `now` epoch tick so the expiry countdown re-renders. The card is
  ALWAYS rendered (operator-grade visibility) and intensifies with severity:
      severityFor: authenticated===false ⇒ 'disconnected';
                   no/!finite expiry      ⇒ 'unknown';
                   days<0 ⇒ 'expired'; days<=7 ⇒ 'warn'; else 'ok'.
      TONE map   : per-severity bar color/opacity, shield icon (ShieldCheck/ShieldAlert/ShieldX),
                   Badge label + variant (success/warning/danger/neutral).
      detail     : disconnected / expiry-unknown / expiry-unparseable / expired-today / expired-Nd-ago /
                   expires-today / expires-in-1-day / expires-in-N-days.
      CTA Link   : to "/tesla-account"; label "Re-authenticate" when expired|disconnected, else "Manage".
  Prompt "Data sources: (none — pure presentational component)" — so there is NO data-state holder here
  (same disposition the predecessor ToolCard surface recorded). The web "states" that DO exist are the five
  severity branches; every one is reproduced as a fully-rendered, non-blank card. `unknown` (awaiting /
  unparseable expiry) and `disconnected` (no account) are the friendly empty/offline surfaces the Apple HIG
  states contract asks for.

