PARITY MAPPING (web → Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind ported)
  GlassPanel(overflow-hidden) → VStack(spacing:0){ flush accent bar; padded content } over the SAME shared
                                TSMaterial.panel + Color.TS.border + TSRadius.lg primitives `tsGlassPanel()`
                                itself uses, then clipShape(rounded) for `overflow-hidden`. (TSGlassPanel
                                bakes in content padding that would inset the flush bar, so the surface is
                                composed from the same design-system material rather than the wrapper.)
  h3 "Tesla account"          → Text(verbatim:) Font.TS.body semibold, Color.TS.textPrimary.
  Badge variant               → TeslaAuthTone → Color.TS.{statusSuccess/statusWarning/statusDanger/textMuted};
                                a compact capsule mirroring TSBadge but for a runtime-localized String label.
  Lucide ShieldCheck/Alert/X  → SF Symbols checkmark.shield.fill / exclamationmark.shield.fill / xmark.shield.fill.
  tone.bar (/40,/50,/60)      → accent-tone color at severity.barOpacity (0.40 / 0.50 / 0.60), flush top bar.
  <Link to="/tesla-account">  → a real Button(onManage) (DI; parent wires navigation) styled as the accent
                                external-link pill, 44pt min target; route exposed as
                                TeslaAuthCardSurface.accountRoute for the contract test.
  `now` tick                  → TimelineView(.periodic(by: 60s)) so the countdown stays live without a hook.
  i18n                        → every rendered string flows through the P1/S10 facade (table "TeslaAuthCard");
                                zero English literals in code (only catalog fallbacks). The lone prompt-listed
                                key "Tesla account" + all badge/detail/CTA strings have catalog keys.
  a11y                        → bar + icon .accessibilityHidden; title+badge+detail folded into ONE VoiceOver
                                header element ("Tesla account, <badge>. <detail>"); CTA is its own labelled
                                Button element; Dynamic Type via the shared Font.TS ramp; no motion (reduce-
